{
  "title": "G2 RPO-A: Guided Group Relative Policy Optimization with Adaptive Guidance",
  "authors": [
    "Yongxin Guo",
    "Wenbo Deng",
    "Zhenglin Cheng",
    "Xiaoying Tang"
  ],
  "year": 2025,
  "arxivId": "2508.13023",
  "abstract": "This paper introduces G2 RPO-A, an adaptive algorithm that enhances the performance of small-size language models (SLMs) in Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable Rewards (RLVR) by injecting ground-truth guidance into roll-out trajectories. Through a comprehensive study of guidance configurations, the authors develop an auto-tuned approach that dynamically adjusts guidance strength based on the model's evolving training dynamics, leading to substantial performance gains over vanilla GRPO.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "The success of Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable Rewards (RLVR) in large language models (LLMs) is hindered in small-size language models (SLMs) due to their limited capacity. <strong>Guided Group Relative Policy Optimization (G2 RPO-A)</strong> addresses this by incorporating ground-truth guidance into roll-out trajectories, facilitating the generation of high-quality candidates. However, <strong>naive guidance</strong> fails to improve performance due to low advantage, necessitating a more nuanced approach.",
