    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "G2 RPO-A formulates Guided GRPO as an optimization problem, where the <strong>guidance ratio</strong> and <strong>guidance length</strong> are crucial parameters. The algorithm dynamically adjusts the guidance length based on the model's real-time learning state, using the <strong>average reward</strong> of recent training steps to determine the next batch's difficulty. This adaptive approach allows the model to learn effectively from both easy and hard examples.",
      "visualization": {
        "type": "flow-diagram",
        "description": "Illustrating the G2 RPO-A pipeline, including the splitting of roll-outs into guided and unguided sets, the comparison of current rewards with previous steps, and the adjustment of guidance length based on the resulting ratio.",
